WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.700
Hello, I'm Marcy Collier-Overstreet, president of the Atlanta City Council.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:10.500
On behalf of the entire city of Atlanta, I'm honored to be part of Celebration 120.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.800
2026 represents a historical milestone in golf's Black history.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.800
Clearview Golf Course, also known as America's Course,

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.900
would celebrate its 80th year of continuous operation by the family of William Powell,

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:28.700
a U.S. Army veteran who could not play golf at public golf courses upon his return

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.600
from serving our country, so he built his own.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.600
Similarly, the National Black Golf Hall of Fame, founded by Harold Donovan,

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.900
and now run by his son Jeff, celebrates its 40th anniversary.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:47.400
These two organizations have come together collectively to celebrate this historical moment.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.400
120 years celebrating golf's Black history.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:01:00.900
City of Atlanta is in the midst of a total renovation of its historic John A. White Golf Course,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.700
where Jeff Donovan serves as its general manager.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:11.800
John A. White will be the permanent home of the National Black Golf Hall of Fame

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:17.000
and will host the hall's 2027 induction weekend.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.500
Obviously, the city is excited and honored to welcome the National Black Golf Hall of Fame

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.000
to Atlanta's storied and illustrious history.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.600
We encourage each of you to support the celebration

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.500
120 event on Friday and Saturday, October 2nd and 3rd,

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:40.500
at Historic Clearview Golf Course in East Canton, Ohio.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:45.600
To celebrate this historic golf moment, and it goes without saying,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.100
when in Atlanta, come to the new John A. White and play around.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.600
So join us in celebrating golf's Black history.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:58.000
And remember, keep it in the short grass.
